-- title:
--   Original BV C1 compact localisation gives the exact unconditional compensated H stopped physical-grid cells
-- statement:
--   The full original stopped compensated H kernel for the bounded-variation spectrally negative Lévy process and original admissible dividend strategy equals the original finite physical-grid signed negative-mark cell source almost surely, for every physical mesh at a chosen finite ruin/horizon T. The theorem extracts all analytic compact-band conditions from the original proved BV C1 localisation certificate, establishes H integrability without arbitrary hypotheses, then instantiates the existing exact H integral finite-cell source theorem with the same actual original Lévy path and dividend clock. Zero and the final ruin/horizon contact are handled by the original (0,u] cells.

